direct-no-ceremony
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-15
what: operator's ask (2026-09-15): `direct` auto-colouring without
  `import scala.language.implicitConversions` and without `import
  Direct.given`. Not `into` (parameter positions only; the block colours
  at ascriptions, receivers and foreign arguments). Measured with scalac:
  the missing import is a feature WARNING, `-language:implicitConversions`
  removes it — one line in ThisBuild / scalacOptions, nine source imports
  go. `Direct.given`: selfColor moves into Free's companion (the implicit
  scope of Conversion[Free[R, A], A]), still gated by DirectCtx; opColor
  stays opt-in in Direct. TestDirectDeep drops both imports as the proof.
files: build.sbt, src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/main/scala/Free.scala,
  the nine files importing implicitConversions, specs/direct-auto-coloring.md,
  CHANGELOG.md
